  "IMP synthesis"
 ],
 "summary": "Cytosol, mainly liver. The purine ring is built on ribose-5-phosphate (as PRPP): glutamine-PRPP amidotransferase is rate-limiting. Ring atoms come from glycine, aspartate, glutamine, CO₂ and two N¹⁰-formyl-THF — so folate antagonists (methotrexate, trimethoprim, sulfonamides) slow purine synthesis. IMP branches to AMP (needs GTP) and GMP (needs ATP), balancing the two. Drugs: 6-mercaptopurine/azathioprine (block de novo synthesis), mycophenolate and ribavirin (IMP dehydrogenase). Salvage by HGPRT recycles hypoxanthine and guanine; HGPRT deficiency = Lesch-Nyhan syndrome.",
